# The built site. 03 regenerates it in seconds from the computed data, so it
# is output, not source.
outputs/03_site/

# outputs/02_dashboard_data/ IS committed, and is the only large thing in the
# repository (about 36 MB). It is what lets a clone, and the GitHub Action
# that publishes the beta, build the site without the 25-minute statistics
# step or the location file that step needs. Every run of 02 rewrites it, so
# each adds its size to history: commit it when the numbers change, not on
# every run.

# The unreleased survey files carry names, addresses, phone numbers, emails
# and exact coordinates, and do not belong in this project. Listed so that one
# copied in by mistake cannot be committed: a file committed once stays in
# history after it is deleted.
S3OK_MSISNet_Wave_[0-9]_Survey_Data.csv
S3OK_MSISNet_Wave_*_Shared_County_Data.csv

# Respondent locations, displaced for sharing but keyed by the same p_id as
# the public wave files, so anyone holding both could place a respondent's
# answers on a map. The site draws its dots from this file; the repository
# does not carry it. Ask the project for a copy to run step 02.
data/S3OK_MSISNet_Wave_1_8_Shared_Location_Data.csv

# R session state and OS files
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
